hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8266","Sheikh Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih and Sheikh Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl told us, saying: Bishr ibn Musa reported Al-Asadi, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Abdul Rabbuh bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Amra bint Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, If the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would complain about something or if he had an ulcer or wound, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said With his finger like this - and he placed his index finger on the ground and then raised it -: “In the name of God, the soil of our land is the saliva of some of us. Our sick will be healed, by permission.” “Our Lord.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8266 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8267","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Usayd bin Asim told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, Ma’bad bin Khalid told me, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Shaddad speaking, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to seek protection from “The eye.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8267 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8268","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told me, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Abu Bakr bin Ja’far al-Quta’i said: Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Zaid bin told us Al-Hubab, Abdul Rahman bin Thabit bin Thuban told us, on the authority of Umair bin Hani, that he heard Junada bin Abi Umayyah Al-Kindi, saying: I heard Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may God be pleased with him, narrating, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that Gabriel, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to him while he was He was feeling ill, so he said: “In the name of God, I perform ruqyah for you from everything that is harming you, from every envy and envious person, and from every grief, and in the name of God, He will heal you.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs, and they did not take it out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8268 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8269","Ahmad bin Ya’qub al-Thaqafi told us, Yusuf bin Ya’qub al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami told us, Amr bin Ali al-Muqaddami told me, On the authority of Abu Janab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, Ubayy bin Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, narrated to me, he said: I was With the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, a Bedouin came and said: O Prophet of God, I have a brother who is suffering from an ailment. He said: “What is his ailment?” He said: There is a sign of it. He said: “Bring it to me.” So he brought it to him and placed it in his hands. “So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, protected him with the opening of the book and four verses.” From the end of Surat Al-Baqarah, and these two verses: {And your God is one God; there is no god but He, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} [Al-Baqarah: 163], and the verse of the Throne, And a verse from Al-Imran: {Allah bears witness that there is no god but Him} [Al-Imran: 18], and a verse from Al-A’raf: {Indeed, your Lord is God who created the heavens. And the earth}, and the last of Surah Al-Mu’minun: {So exalted is God, the True King} [Al-Mu’minun: 116], and a verse from Surat Al-Jinn: {And indeed, the Most High is the grandfather of our Lord. He has taken a companion or a son} [Al-Jinn: 3], and ten verses from the beginning of As-Saffat, and three verses from the last of Surah Al-Hashr, and Say, He is God, One. And the two exorcists, “Then the man stood up as if he had never doubted anything.” The two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, argued as evidence by narrating this hadith, all of them on the authority of The last of them is other than Abu Janab al-Kalbi, and the hadith is preserved and authentic, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8269 - The hadith is objectionable"
"8270","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Dhuli told us, Musaddad told us, Abdul-Wahid told us Bin Ziyad, Uthman bin Hakim told me, my grandmother Al-Rabbab told me, she said: I heard Sahl bin Hunaif, saying: We passed by a flood, so I went in and washed myself. So I went out with a fever, and it was reported to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “See Abu Thabit seeking refuge.” He said: So I said: Oh my lord. Is the ruqyah valid? He said: “There is no ruqyah except for a sore throat or a fever or a bite.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8270 - True"
"8271","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Muhammad bin Saeed Al-Asbahani told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Abbas Ibn Dhurayh, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Anas, who narrated it, saying: “There is no ruqyah except for an eye, or a fever, or blood that cannot be shed.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. Muslim, and they did not expel him.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8271 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8272","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Yusuf bin Atiya told us, he said: I sat with Yazid al-Raqqashi, and I heard him say: Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, told us that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was... He was afflicted with ophthalmia, or one of his family and friends prayed with these words: “O God, grant me the benefit of my sight, make it my heir, and show me My revenge is on the enemy, and grant me victory over those who wronged me.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8272 - It contains two weak hadiths"
"8273","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Ju’fi told us, Talaq bin Ghanam told us, Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Habba, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Whoever says when he sneezes, he will hear it: Praise be to God for everything.” Immediately, there was no toothache or earache.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8273 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8274","Muhammad bin Hani told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah and Al-Fadl bin Muhammad told us, they said: Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Abi Habiba, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to teach them of pain and fever, saying: “In the name of God the Great, we seek refuge in God the Great from the evil of the race of disgrace and from the evil of “Here is the fire.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"8275","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Dhuhli told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Sufyan, and Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, And Abu Hudhayfah said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Sulayman bin Abi Hathamah, on the authority of Hafsa, that A woman from the Quraysh called Al-Shifa’ was performing ruqyah for an ant, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Teach her Hafsa.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8275 - True"
"8276","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Malhan told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, On the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Urwa told me, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw Umm Salamah’s house. The wife of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, married a slave girl with a white mark on her face, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “She has a look, so look for her.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8276 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8277","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Muhadhar bin Al-Muwari told us, Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, said: A man from the Ansar called Amr bin Hazm came. He was performing ruqyah from the snake, so he said: O Messenger of God, you have forbidden the ruqyah, and I am performing ruqyah from the snake. He said: “Tell it to me,” so he told it to him. He said: “There is no harm in these covenants.” He said: A man from the Ansar came and was performing ruqyah for the scorpion, so he said: O Messenger of God, you have forbidden Concerning ruqyah, “And I am more ruqyah than a scorpion.” He said: “Whoever is able to benefit his brother should do so.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and he did not \"He takes him out\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8277 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8278","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Zuhair bin Harb told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah, Asim Ibn Bahdala told us, on the authority of Zirr Ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ The nations were presented to me during the season, and I saw all of them, and I was impressed by their abundance and majesty. They filled the plain and the mountains, and it was said: Which Muhammad are you satisfied with? So I say: Yes, O Lord, and he said: Indeed, you have with these seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without being called to account, and they are the ones who do not seek enslavement and do not conceal themselves. And in their Lord they put their trust.” Then Okasha bin Muhsin stood up and said: O Messenger of God, pray to God to make me one of them. So he called for him, and a man stood up. Another, and he said: O Messenger of God, pray to God to make me one of them, and he said: “Okasha preceded you to it.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration from some aspects. And they did not give it away, and there is no prohibition against performing ruqyah. Trusting in it did not have any effect, and there is evidence for that.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8278 - True"
"8279","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh did not narrate to us. Abu Bakr said: He informed us, and Ali said: Bishr bin Musa narrated to us. Al-Humaidi, on the authority of Sufyan, Ibn Abi Najih told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Al-Ghaffar ibn Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He who seeks guidance or conceals himself does not rely on him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8279 - True"
"8280","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Shayban Al-Ayli told us, Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Whoever says in the evening: I seek refuge in the words of God Complete protection from the evil of what He created three times, no living creature harmed Him that night.” He said: And when a person was stung by his family, he said the words. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it in this context.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8280 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8281","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Malazim bin Amr told us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih and Ahmad ibn Ja’far al-Quta’i narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, narrated to us Ali bin Al-Madini, Mulazim bin Amr told us, Abdullah bin Badr told us, on the authority of Qais bin Talq, on the authority of his father, “He was stung by a scorpion when The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, separated it and wiped it with his hand. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8281 - True"
"8282","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Abu Khalid bin Yazid bin Abdul Rahman Al-Dalani told us, Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hassan Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever visits a sick person whose death has not come, he says to him seven times: I ask God Almighty, Lord of the Great Throne. That he will heal you and make you well, unless God protects him from that disease. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it after they agreed on The hadith of Al-Minhal bin Amr, with its chain of transmission, he used to seek refuge with Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8282 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8283","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi informed us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, that three people came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “Indeed, a companion of ours.” We are sick and were prescribed cauterization. Should we cauterize it? He remained silent, then returned. Then he said the third time: “Hot it if you wish, and if you wish, water it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. And they did not take him out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8283 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8284","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz Al-Baghawi told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Abu Al-Tayyah told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade “About cauterization, so we suffered, but we did not succeed, nor did we succeed.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration on the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8284 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8285","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi informed me, Muawiyah ibn Amr told us, Muawiyah ibn Amr told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Ubayy ibn Ka’b was thrown into his ankle, so he sent The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent him a doctor to heal him.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8285 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8286","Yazid bin Zuray’ told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, cauterized As’ad bin “a prick from a thorn”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8286 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8287","Zuhayr bin Muawiyah told us, Abu Al-Zubayr told us, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “Saad bin Muadh was shot in the ankle, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, crushed it with his hand.” With a mishqas, he said: Then she threw it, so he decided it the second time: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8287 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8288","Ahmad bin Ya’qub al-Thaqafi told me, Yusuf bin Ya’qub al-Qadi told me, Omar bin Marzuq told us, Imran al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: “Abu Talha and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were among us among us, but I was not forbidden.” This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8288 - True"
"8289","Abu Amr Ismail bin Nujaid Al-Sulami and Abu Sa’id Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, saying: Abu Muslim told us, Abu Sa’id told us Asim, on the authority of Haywa bin Shurayh, on the authority of Khalid bin Ubaid, on the authority of Musharrah bin Haaan, on the authority of Utba bin Amir, may God be pleased with him, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wears an amulet, God will not grant him peace, and whoever wears an amulet, God will not complete it.” This hadith is with an authentic chain of narration, and it was not \"He takes him out\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8289 - True"
"8290","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Al-Hasan bin Ahmed told us, Jeddi Ahmed bin Abi Shuaib told us, Musa bin Ayyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Kufi, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utba Ibn Masoud, on the authority of Zainab, Abdullah’s wife, said that she was afflicted with redness in her face, so an old woman came in and tore a thread and hung it. On it, so Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, entered and saw it on it, and said: What is this? She said: I had radiant redness, so he extended his hand and cut it off, then said: Indeed, the family of Abdullah is free from polytheism. She said: Then he said: Indeed, the Messenger of God God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told us: “Indeed, incantations, amulets, and guardianship are polytheism.” He said: So I said: What is guardianship? He said: “Tawliya is the one who excites men.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8290 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8291","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mawjih informed me, Abdan informed me, Abdullah informed me, Talha bin Abi informed me Saeed, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said: “Amulets are what “It was hung before the calamity descended, and whatever was hung after it is not an amulet.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8291 - True"
"8292","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Muslim bin Abi Shuaib Al-Harrani told us, Miskin told us. Ibn Bukayr, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Raja’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about Al-Nashrah, and he said: “They were mentioned in the presence of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” “And he acknowledged that it is the work of Satan.” This is an authentic hadith, and Abu Raja’ is Matar al-Warraq, and they did not bring him out.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8292 - True"
